<%#
Cistergraphia: the scriptorium (fol. 2v)
========================================

Purpose:
- The reader's game. A game plate brought to Read opens as its puzzle: the
  reading desk for an intact one, the bench to restore a worn one, the board
  to rejoin a broken one. The decoder's answer stays one click away, below

Design Decisions:
- The page is built from the file alone, never from the message: which signs
  are worn, what their strokes allow, where the fragments' edges are. The
  scribe's plate page knows more; this one cannot, and says so
- The same bench, board and plate figure as the plate page (partials), so the
  two pages play the same. On a wide screen the plate and the work sit side
  by side (.room), the plate held in view while the desk, the bench or the
  notebook scrolls: what is read is never a scroll away from where it is read
- "Decipher it" posts the same file back with decipher=1: the solver, for a
  reader who wants the answer, or has one to check
- A plate won (read to the end, every pair balanced, whole again) is counted
  in the scriptorium record, by rung (data-play), kept in the browser; the
  reserved line says so

Constraints:
- Worn plates under a grille play once the key is given; broken plates
  follow the snail. Sealed plates are not games
- A plate with a tablet of its own opens at the desk with the notebook
  under it (intact only); the page holds its sums, never its tablet, and the
  scribe (POST /ask) confirms. Pathless too, it is the expert plate: two
  things to find, in order. The notebook waits shut until the desk finds the
  way on sums alone (its sums would tell the way), then opens on that way's
  sums, built by the page
- A ruined plate is the board first, then (rejoined=1, from the board once
  whole) the bench on the plate drawn whole from its own fragments; the file
  carried on to the decoder is still the broken one
- The day's chapter (@chapter, web/chapter.rb) is this page on the abbey's
  plate of the day: a line says which chapter, which day and which rung; its
  source shows once it is read, and the record counts the chapters read. A
  ruined chapter's board asks the chapter itself for its bench
%>
<% rung = if @broken || @rejoined then @weathered ? 'ruined' : 'broken'
          elsif @expert then 'expert'
          elsif @grid then 'pathless'
          elsif @notebook then 'tablet'
          elsif @desk then 'intact'
          else 'worn'
          end %>
<section class="leaf" aria-labelledby="play-title" data-play="<%= rung %>"<% if @chapter %> data-chapter="<%= @chapter.date.iso8601 %>"<% end %>>
  <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 2<sup>v</sup></p>
  <% if @chapter %>
    <p class="chapter-mark"><span class="chapter-number">Chapter <%= @chapter.number %></span> · <%= chapter_day(@chapter) %><% if @chapter.feast %> · <span class="chapter-feast"><%= @chapter.feast %></span><% end %></p>
  <% end %>
  <h1 id="play-title" class="rubric"><%= if @broken then @weathered ? 'A plate to rejoin and restore' : 'A plate to rejoin'
                                            elsif @desk then 'A plate to read'
                                            else 'A plate to restore'
                                            end %></h1>
  <% if @rejoined %>
    <p class="lede">Whole again: the fragments are rejoined, and the plate has lost <%= @entries.size %> <%= @entries.size == 1 ? 'stroke position' : 'stroke positions' %>, hatched where the surface is worn. Now restore it: press the lost digits back in, each pair of signs must sum to a value on the tablet, and where two or three letters balance, the words decide.</p>
  <% elsif @grid && !@desk %>
    <p class="lede">The plate is worn and pathless: <%= @values.size / 2 %> pairs of signs, <%= pathless_lacunae(@worn) %> <%= pathless_lacunae(@worn) == 1 ? 'stroke position' : 'stroke positions' %> lost where the surface is hatched, and nothing says which way it runs. Choose one of the five ways at the bench: along it the pairs form, and read as letters or do not. Along the way, press the lost digits back in: each pair must sum to a value on the tablet, and where two or three letters balance, the words decide.</p>
  <% elsif @expert %>
    <p class="lede">The plate is whole, pathless, and has a tablet of its own: <%= @values.size / 2 %> pairs of signs, and nothing says which way they run, nor what their sums read. First the way: choose one of the five at the desk and read along it. Every pair sums to a value of the tablet, whatever the tablet, and along a wrong way one soon does not. Three pairs that land open the notebook on every sum the way makes. Then the tablet: write letters in pencil, and the scribe confirms them three at a time.</p>
  <% elsif @grid %>
    <p class="lede">The plate is whole and pathless: <%= @values.size / 2 %> pairs of signs, but nothing says which way it runs. Choose one of the five ways at the desk and read along it: the pairs form, and each sums to a letter on the tablet, or does not. Along the wrong way the letters stop; the notebook keeps what each way gave.</p>
  <% elsif @notebook %>
    <p class="lede">The plate is whole and has a tablet of its own: <%= @notebook.size %> sums, each one letter, but not the letter the shared tablet gives it. Build its tablet in the notebook. Every pair that adds to one sum is the same letter, however it is spelled; the sum seen most is usually the space, or <i>e</i>. Write a letter in pencil against a sum and the text below takes it at once. Ask the scribe: entries are confirmed three at a time, never one.</p>
  <% elsif @desk %>
    <p class="lede">The plate is whole: <%= @values.size / 2 %> pairs of signs, each summing to a letter on the tablet. Read it pair by pair: type what each sign reads and the page adds them. Guided, a tap on a sign shows its value; unaided, a wrong reading is marked, never corrected, and three in a row earn the Lectio’s ranks.</p>
  <% elsif @broken && @weathered %>
    <p class="lede">The plate came in <%= fragments_count(@fragments.size) %>, worn where the surface is hatched. Lay them on the board, turned where need be: a join holds when every pair of signs can balance, whatever its lacunae held. Whole again, it reads as an edition, and the bench opens on it to restore what is lost.</p>
  <% elsif @broken %>
    <p class="lede">The plate came in <%= fragments_count(@fragments.size) %>. Lay them on the board, turned where need be: only one arrangement makes every pair of signs balance, and the shapes alone will not tell you which.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="lede">The plate has lost <%= @entries.size %> <%= @entries.size == 1 ? 'stroke position' : 'stroke positions' %>, hatched where the surface is worn. Press the lost digits back in: each pair of signs must sum to a value on the tablet. Where two or three letters balance, the words decide.</p>
  <% end %>

  <% if @chapter %>
    <p class="chapter-week"><%= chapter_week(@chapter) %></p>
  <% end %>

  <dl class="specs">
    <div><dt>Signs</dt><dd><%= @size * @size %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Grid</dt><dd><%= @size %> × <%= @size %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Layout</dt><dd><%= if @broken then 'Phaistos'
                                  elsif @grid then 'Withheld: one of the five ways'
                                  else layout_name(@layout)
                                  end %></dd></div>
    <% if @broken %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd><%= @weathered ? "Ruined: #{fragments_count(@fragments.size)}, worn" : "Broken, in #{fragments_count(@fragments.size)}" %></dd></div>
    <% elsif @rejoined %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Ruined, rejoined: worn</dd></div>
    <% elsif @grid && !@desk %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd><%= @tally ? 'Worn, pathless, with tally signs' : 'Worn, pathless' %></dd></div>
    <% elsif @grid %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Intact, pathless</dd></div>
      <% if @expert %><div><dt>Tablet</dt><dd>Its own: to build</dd></div><% end %>
    <% elsif @notebook %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Intact</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tablet</dt><dd>Its own: to build</dd></div>
    <% elsif @desk %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Intact</dd></div>
    <% else %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd><%= @tally ? 'Worn, with tally signs' : 'Worn' %></dd></div>
    <% end %>
    <% if grille? %>
      <div><dt>Grille key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout %></code></dd></div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>

  <% if @broken %>
    <%== erb :_board, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, fragments: @fragments, size: @size, worn: @weathered } %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="room">
      <div class="room-plate">
        <% if @grid %>
          <%== erb :_plate, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, cells: pathless_cells_json(@grid), geometry: plate_layout_json(@values, @layout), layout: @layout, decoy: nil, size: @size, grid: @grid } %>
        <% elsif @desk %>
          <%== erb :_plate, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, cells: plate_cells_json(@values, @layout), geometry: plate_layout_json(@values, @layout), layout: @layout, decoy: nil, size: @size } %>
        <% else %>
          <%== erb :_plate, layout: false, locals: { svg: @plate_svg || @svg_content, cells: plate_cells_json(@values, @layout, @damage), geometry: plate_layout_json(@values, @layout), layout: @layout, decoy: nil, size: @size } %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="room-work">
        <% if @grid && !@desk %>
          <%== erb :_bench, layout: false, locals: { entries: @entries, values: @values, damage: @damage, tally: @tally, pathless: true, worn: @worn } %>
        <% elsif @grid %>
          <%== erb :_desk, layout: false, locals: { values: @values, tablet: @expert ? {} : Cistergraphia::CHARACTERS, pathless: true, own: @expert } %>
          <% if @expert %><%== erb :_notebook, layout: false, locals: { entries: [], values: @values, shut: true } %><% end %>
        <% elsif @notebook %>
          <%== erb :_desk, layout: false, locals: { values: @values, tablet: {}, own: true } %>
          <%== erb :_notebook, layout: false, locals: { entries: @notebook, values: @values } %>
        <% elsif @desk %>
          <%== erb :_desk, layout: false, locals: { values: @values, tablet: Cistergraphia::CHARACTERS } %>
        <% else %>
          <%== erb :_bench, layout: false, locals: { entries: @entries, values: @values, damage: @damage, tally: @tally } %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <p class="record" data-record="play" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <% if @chapter %>
    <p class="chapter-source" data-chapter-source hidden>From <%= @chapter.source %>.</p>
  <% end %>

  <form class="readback" method="post" action="/decode">
    <h2 class="index-heading">Ask the decoder</h2>
    <input type="hidden" name="svg" value="<%= @svg_content %>">
    <input type="hidden" name="decipher" value="1">
    <% if grille? %><input type="hidden" name="grille" value="<%= @layout %>"><% end %>
    <div class="readback-row">
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Decipher it</button>
      <% if @layout == :rongorongo %>
        <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="turn-plate" aria-pressed="false">Turn the plate</button>
      <% end %>
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/decode">Read another</a>
    </div>
  </form>

  <% if @chapter %>
    <% before = Chapter.of(@chapter.date - 1)
       after = Chapter.of(@chapter.date + 1) %>
    <% if before || after %>
      <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Chapters">
        <% if before %><a href="<%= before.path %>">Chapter <%= before.number %>, the day before</a><% end %>
        <% if after %><a class="chapter-nav-after" href="<%= after.path %>">Chapter <%= after.number %>, the day after</a><% end %>
      </nav>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</section>
